        "field": "abstract",
        "raw_text": "The best existing pairing-based traitor tracing schemes have O( √ N)-sized parameters, which has stood since 2006. This intuitively seems to be consistent with the fact that pairings allow for degree-2 computations, yielding a quadratic compression. In this work, we show that this intuition is false by building a traitor tracing scheme from pairings with O( 3√ N)-sized parameters. We addi- tionally give schemes with a variety of parameter size trade-offs, including a scheme with constant-size ciphertexts and public keys (but linear-sized secret keys). We obtain our schemes by developing a number of new traitor tracing techniques, giving the first significant parameter improve- ments in pairings-based traitor tracing in over a decade.",
